    "committer": "GitHub <noreply@github.com>",
    "message": "fix: keep the roxygen examples off the network (#164)\n\nparseAndValidateGenomeSpec() and the GWASTrack constructor both validate\ntheir inputs with httr::http_error(), so two example blocks queried\ngladki.pl on every R CMD check - ours, and Bioconductor's build machines.\nThis is the same failure #163 fixed in the vignette; nothing masked it in\nthe examples, since R/ carried no \\dontrun or \\donttest at all.\n\nThe custom genome example now reads inst/extdata/sarsGenome, which ships\nthe same fasta, index and gff3 the example used to fetch, so it still\nruns. The remote GWAS example is wrapped in \\donttest, as a remote source\nis the point of that block.",
    "time": 1785573782
  },
